1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,810
Adding forever,
and the answer is 1?

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,680
A square with an area of 1

3
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:07,500
Color in half: 1/2

4
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:09,320
Half of what's left: 1/4

5
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:12,890
Half of what's left again… and on and on!

6
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:16,760
No matter how long we add, it can't leave the square.
The gap shrinks to 0 → the sum is 1

7
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:17,880
What if it shrinks by 1/4 each time?

8
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:21,050
Only one of the three pieces is yellow,
then repeat in the last corner

9
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:24,820
The three colors share it equally,
so yellow is 1/3 of the whole!

10
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:27,990
(1/2) ÷ (1 − 1/2) = 1
(1/4) ÷ (1 − 1/4) = 1/3

11
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:31,490
If the ratio is less than 1,
an endless sum still has a limit = an infinite geometric series

12
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:36,240
NEXT: A positive test,
but only a 9% chance it's real?
